# MCP Connections — Global Configuration

## Available Servers

| # | Server | MCP Name | Primary Tool |
|---|--------|----------|-------------|
| 1 | Snowflake | `snowflake` | `snowflake_query` (SQL execution) |
| 2 | dbt | `dbt` | `build`, `run`, `test`, `compile`, `show`, `list`, `get_lineage_dev`, `get_node_details_dev` |
| 3 | Salesforce | `salesforce` | `run_soql_query`, `get_username` |
| 4 | Atlassian | `atlassian` | **DEPRECATED for Jira** — use API token + curl per `jira-api-access` rule. (Confluence-only fallback.) |
| 5 | Slack | `plugin-slack-slack` | `mcp_auth` then native tools |
| 6 | Sigma | `sigma` | Sigma dashboard tools |
| 7 | GitHub | `gh` CLI | `gh pr`, `gh issue`, `gh api` (Shell) |

## Google Drive / Sheets — use existing channels, not a Drive MCP

Workday corporate Google accounts have GCP disabled, so the Google Drive MCP cannot be set up. Use these instead:

| Need | Path |
|---|---|
| Read a Fivetran-synced Google Sheet (REF_FIN_CUSTOMIZED_DATA, ACV overrides, etc.) | Snowflake MCP → `BASE_PROD.GOOGLE_SHEETS.*` |
| Read an ad-hoc Google Doc / Slides / un-synced Sheet | Cursor IDE Browser MCP → navigate `https://docs.google.com/...` |
| Stage data into Snowflake from a new sheet | Ask Data Eng to add a Fivetran connector for the sheet |

## Quick Reference

- **Snowflake**: SSO auth (`externalbrowser`), role `ROLE_ANALYTICS_ENGINEER`, warehouse `ANALYTICS_ENGINEER_WH`, default DB `CERTIFIED_DEV`.
- **dbt**: `uvx dbt-mcp`, set `DBT_PROJECT_DIR` per workspace.
- **Salesforce**: `sf-mcp-server`, org `[REDACTED_EMAIL]`, toolset `data`.
- **Atlassian / Jira**: ⚠️ **Always use API token + curl** (see `jira-api-access` rule). Never call the `atlassian` MCP for Jira. Env vars: `JIRA_BASE_URL`, `JIRA_EMAIL`, `JIRA_API_TOKEN` in `~/.zshrc`.
- **Slack**: Built-in plugin, call `mcp_auth` on first use.
- **Sigma**: `npx @getguru/sigma-mcp`, requires `SIGMA_CLIENT_ID` + `SIGMA_CLIENT_SECRET`.
- **GitHub**: `gh auth login` (OAuth), no MCP server needed.

## Setup for New Workspace

```bash
cp ~/.cursor/skills/mcp-connections/mcp-template.json <project>/.cursor/mcp.json
# Edit DBT_PROJECT_DIR, restart Cursor
```

For detailed configs and troubleshooting, see `~/.cursor/skills/mcp-connections/`.
